</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 472)</h2>
<p><b>A wider playlist shows you more of the name.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: the floating playlist ignored the window width.</b> Widening it left empty margins while shot names stayed truncated — which is the one reason you'd widen it. The list now fills the window, so <code>SAA_PR1_070_gen_v004_comp_v002</code> reads in full.</li>
<li><b>New: sort the playlist</b> — by name, date modified, duration, or reverse, from the ⇅ button in the panel header. <b>Groups stay together</b>: a version stack is a unit, and splitting it would break the compare pairing it exists for. The clip you're watching stays the clip you're watching.</li>
<li>Sorting is something you do, not a mode that stays on — review order is a decision, so nothing re-sorts behind you.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
